;;; An activator that binds a value parameter to a nested fact leaves the
;;; parameter unbound — M1f **W33**, register row `W33/activator-nested-value`
;;; (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), banked by S1f.5.0 (2026-11-08) from
;;; S1f.5.5's census (§ Findings outside the grammar; its probe
;;; `activator_nested_value.ein`, the program unchanged), filed `open` and
;;; owned by S1f.5.18, on the user's ruling of 2026-11-08 on the census
;;; (*"Q3 - as recommended"*).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Three `p` facts, one of them over the nested fact `(f a)`, a rule `act`
;;; whose parameter `?y` is an argument of its premise and its conclusion, and
;;; its activator `(act (f a))`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; An activator binds a rule's parameters to its arguments, and a nested fact
;;; is a value as any other: `?y` is `(f a)`, so `act` matches `(p (f a))`
;;; alone and root holds `(hit (f a))` and no other `hit`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The compiler skips a nested fact when it seeds a rule's parameters (*a
;;; nested Fact does not bind*), so `?y` is left free and `act` fires on every
;;; `p`: root holds `(hit a)`, `(hit b)` and `(hit (f a))`, H is empty and R is
;;; {∅}, exit 0 (`ein saturate FILE --dump`, `ein solve FILE` and `ein oracle
;;; FILE` at `ec004a48`, the engine `916d97ac`'s, release and debug alike).
;;; W24 refused the same activator only where the parameter names a relation.

;; An activator binds a rule's parameter, used as an argument, to a nested fact.
(relation p T) (relation hit T)
(p a) (p b) (p (f a))
(rule act (?y) :match (p ?y) :assert (hit ?y))
(act (f a))
(query :goal (hit ?x))
